{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01ATszLmsttNCdanid9noiCF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: go-unix-utils is a specification-driven experiment that derives formal specs from C source code of classic Unix utilities, generates Go implementations via an AI orchestrator, and verifies parity through differential testing against GNU reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture**: Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify) with `cmd/` per-utility packages, `pkg/testutils/` differential testing harness, `pkg/sys/` platform abstractions, `pkg/format/` output formatting, and `magefiles/` build infrastructure. The generation pipeline targets only `cmd/` and `pkg/` directories; `docs/` is human-authored.\n\n**Current state**: Source code exists for all foundational packages (`pkg/testutils`, `pkg/sys`, `pkg/format`) and several utilities (`cmd/cat`, `cmd/du`, `cmd/ls`, `cmd/sponge`, `cmd/wc`, `cmd/version`). Releases 02.0–02.2 have pending specs (no PRDs yet), so code generation is blocked for those.\n\n**Earliest incomplete release**: rel01.1 (cat). The implementation (`cmd/cat/main.go`) covers R1–R5 of prd006-cat, but the test file (`cmd/cat/cat_test.go`) only covers R1.1, R1.2, R5.2, R5.3. Line numbering (R2), squeeze (R3), and display features (R4) are implemented but have no differential tests.\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\nPer P1, I focus on the earliest incomplete release. Releases 00.0 through 01.3 and 03.0–04.0 have source code, but rel01.1 (cat) has a clear test coverage gap: the implementation handles R2 (line numbering), R3 (squeeze), and R4 (display transforms), but cat_test.go only tests R1 and R5. Per P2 and P5, tests follow implementation, and since the implementation is complete, the next task is tests. Per P8, I order implementation before tests, but implementation is already done, so tests are next.\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"cmd/cat differential tests for prd006-cat R2.1, R2.3, R3.1, R4.3\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/prd006-cat.yaml (R2 line numbering, R3 squeeze, R4 display requirements)\n      - cmd/cat/cat_test.go (existing differential test pattern -- TestMain, writeTestFile, normalizeProgramName, DiffTest usage)\n      - cmd/cat/main.go (implementation of line numbering, squeeze, and display features under test)\n      - pkg/testutils/difftest.go (DiffTest struct and RunDiffTests API)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/cat/cat_test.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add differential tests for line numbering (-n, -b), squeeze (-s), and end markers (-E)\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Add differential test for prd006-cat R2.1: cat -n numbers all output lines with the format \\\"%6d\\\\t\\\" prefix, comparing Go binary output byte-for-byte against gcat -n on single-file and multi-line inputs including blank lines\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Add differential test for prd006-cat R2.3: cat -b numbers only non-blank output lines, and when both -b and -n are given, -b overrides -n -- verify by comparing against gcat with both flag combinations\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Add differential test for prd006-cat R3.1: cat -s squeezes runs of consecutive blank lines down to a single blank line, verified against gcat -s on input containing two or more consecutive blank lines\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Add differential test for prd006-cat R4.3: cat -E appends a $ character at the end of each output line before the newline, verified against gcat -E\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Follow the existing test pattern in cat_test.go: each test function calls testutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBinary, refBinary, []testutils.DiffTest{...}), uses t.Parallel(), and creates test input files via the existing writeTestFile helper in t.TempDir()\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Reuse the existing TestMain setup -- goBinary and refBinary are package-level vars set by TestMain which builds the Go binary and locates gcat via exec.LookPath. Do not duplicate or modify TestMain\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Each test function creates input files with content specifically designed to exercise the feature: for line numbering, include files with a mix of blank and non-blank lines; for squeeze, include files with 3+ consecutive blank lines; for end markers, include lines with varying content including empty lines\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"A TestCatLineNumbering function exists that runs at least 2 DiffTest cases exercising -n with a single file containing blank and non-blank lines, and passes by matching gcat -n output byte-for-byte\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"A TestCatNumberNonblank function exists that runs at least 2 DiffTest cases: one with -b alone on input containing blank lines, and one with both -b and -n flags to verify -b overrides -n. Both pass by matching gcat output\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"A TestCatSqueeze function exists that runs at least 2 DiffTest cases exercising -s on input with consecutive blank lines, and passes by matching gcat -s output byte-for-byte\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"A TestCatShowEnds function exists that runs at least 2 DiffTest cases exercising -E on varied input, and passes by matching gcat -E output byte-for-byte\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"go test ./cmd/cat/... passes with all new and existing tests (no regressions in TestCatFileRead, TestCatStdinRead, TestCatErrorHandling)\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":82403,"cache_read_input_tokens":19289,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":82403},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},